{%- comment -%}
  snippets/portal-section.liquid — one section's root, templates, skeleton and live
  region (spec task 19.4, design §16.2, §18.8, §21.6).

  Requirements 15.1, 16.1, 6.3.

  ── WHY ONE SNIPPET FOR TEN SECTIONS ──────────────────────────────────────────
  Every section needs the same five things, and each of them is a contract with the
  task-18 primitives:

    `data-portal-section`        the boot scan's selector (core.ts)
    `data-portal-live`           the region `ui/announce.ts` finds; it MUST be
                                 server-rendered, because a region injected at
                                 announcement time is not reliably announced (§20.6)
    `data-portal-state-message`  where `render/states.ts` writes the state's prose
    `data-portal-reference`      where §22.9's shortened request reference goes
    `data-portal-retry`          the control `render/states.ts` binds and unbinds

  Ten copies of that scaffold would be ten chances for one attribute to be
  misspelled, and a misspelled `data-portal-live` fails silently — the section works
  and only a screen reader user notices. One snippet, one vocabulary.

  ── THE SKELETON CARRIES FINAL GEOMETRY (Requirement 16.1, §21.6) ─────────────
  `data-state="loading"` is set here, in the markup, so the first paint is the
  designed loading state rather than an empty box that jumps when data arrives. The
  skeleton rows reserve the same height as real rows, which is what keeps CLS at 0 —
  the measured desktop layout shift of 0.1044 on the current account page is the
  defect this pattern exists to avoid repeating.

  ── ROW TEMPLATES ARE MARKUP, NOT STRINGS ─────────────────────────────────────
  `render/rows.ts` clones a `<template>` and fills `[data-slot]` with
  `textContent`. The markup therefore lives here, in Liquid, where it is reviewable
  and where a product title can never become an element (§5.3 records that the
  current wishlist builds rows with `innerHTML`; NB-14).

  A section whose own task has not landed yet gets the scaffold and no row
  template. That is deliberate: an empty `<template>` that pretends to be a row
  shape would be worse than its absence, because `rows.ts` would clone it and
  render blank rows rather than failing loudly.

  PARAMETERS
    name        the `data-portal-section` value
    empty_text  optional override for the empty state's prose
{%- endcomment -%}

<section
  class="athoor-portal__section"
  data-portal-section="{{ name }}"
  data-state="loading"
  aria-busy="true"
>
  {%- comment -%} The section-scoped polite region (§20.6). {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="athoor-portal__live" data-portal-live aria-live="polite"></p>

  <div class="athoor-portal__state">
    <p class="athoor-portal__state-message" data-portal-state-message>Preparing your account</p>
    <p class="athoor-portal__state-reference" data-portal-reference hidden></p>
    <button class="athoor-portal__retry" type="button" data-portal-retry hidden>Try again</button>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The skeleton. Three rows is enough to read as a list without implying a count,
    and each reserves a real row's height so nothing shifts when data replaces it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="athoor-portal__skeleton" data-portal-skeleton aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="athoor-portal__skeleton-row"></div>
    <div class="athoor-portal__skeleton-row"></div>
    <div class="athoor-portal__skeleton-row"></div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} Where the section's own module writes its rendered content. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="athoor-portal__section-body" data-portal-body></div>

  {%- case name -%}
    {%- when 'orders' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Task 20.1. The row is a RULED ROW, not a card (§18.5): a hairline and air,
        no border box. Four columns at desktop, stacked with a 64 px thumbnail at
        base, and the total right-aligned on the number's baseline.

        `width`/`height` are set from N1's intrinsic dimensions by the module, and
        the placeholders here are the reserved geometry so nothing shifts when the
        image loads (§21.6) — the measured 0.1044 desktop shift on the current
        account page is what this pattern exists to avoid repeating.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <template data-portal-row="order">
        <li class="athoor-portal__row athoor-orders__row">
          <span class="athoor-portal__image-box athoor-orders__thumb">
            <img
              class="athoor-portal__image"
              data-slot="image"
              alt=""
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              width="64"
              height="64"
              sizes="(min-width: 990px) 80px, 64px"
            >
          </span>
          <a class="athoor-portal__row-link athoor-orders__link" data-slot="link" href="#"></a>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-number" data-slot="number"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="date"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="items"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-total" data-slot="total"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-status" data-slot="status"></span>
        </li>
      </template>

      {%- comment -%}
        "Show earlier orders" (task 20.1). Hidden until the module knows there is
        another page, and it APPENDS — §20.2 requires focus to stay on this control
        and the new count to be announced instead.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button class="athoor-portal__more" type="button" data-portal-more-orders hidden>
        Show earlier orders
      </button>

    {%- when 'order-detail' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Task 20.3. ONE COLUMN AT EVERY WIDTH: an order is a document, read top to
        bottom, and a two-column order confuses the totals with the address.

        The totals are a real `<table>` with a `<caption>`, because they are tabular
        data and a screen reader user needs the row header read with each figure
        (§20.3). The caption is visually hidden, not absent.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <header class="athoor-order__header">
        <h2 class="athoor-order__number" data-slot="number"></h2>
        <p class="athoor-order__date athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="date"></p>
        <p class="athoor-order__fulfilment" data-slot="fulfilment"></p>
        <a class="athoor-order__tracking" data-portal-tracking href="#" hidden></a>
      </header>

      <button class="athoor-portal__action athoor-order__reorder" type="button" data-portal-reorder>
        Reorder everything available
      </button>

      <table class="athoor-order__totals">
        <caption class="athoor-portal__visually-hidden">Order totals</caption>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Subtotal</th><td data-slot="subtotal"></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Delivery</th><td data-slot="shipping"></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Tax</th><td data-slot="tax"></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Total</th><td data-slot="total"></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <section class="athoor-order__delivery">
        <h3 class="athoor-portal__eyebrow">Delivered to</h3>
        {%- comment -%}
          Removed entirely by the module when the order has no shipping address —
          a digital-only order must not render an empty "Delivered to" heading.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="athoor-order__address" data-portal-address></p>
      </section>

      <template data-portal-row="line-item">
        <li class="athoor-portal__row athoor-order__line">
          <span class="athoor-portal__image-box athoor-order__thumb">
            <img class="athoor-portal__image" data-slot="image" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="80" height="80">
          </span>
          {%- comment -%}
            Requirement 6.8/6.9: the link is REMOVED by the module when the product
            has no handle, and the recorded title and price render regardless — which
            is what lets a two-year-old order still read correctly.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <a class="athoor-order__line-link" data-slot="link" href="#"></a>
          <span class="athoor-order__line-title" data-slot="title"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="quantity"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="unit-price"></span>
          <span class="athoor-order__line-total" data-slot="line-total"></span>
          {%- comment -%}
            The availability word. §7.5's four states are conveyed in TEXT, never by
            colour alone (Requirement 17.8).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="athoor-order__line-availability" data-slot="availability"></span>
          <button class="athoor-portal__action athoor-order__buy-again" type="button" data-portal-buy-again>
            Buy again
          </button>
        </li>
      </template>

    {%- when 'wishlist' -%}
      <template data-portal-row="wishlist">
        <li class="athoor-portal__grid-item">
          {%- comment -%}
            The one card-shaped element §18.5 permits in a row: the image needs a
            defined box for its reserved aspect ratio, and it carries no border.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="athoor-portal__image-box">
            <img class="athoor-portal__image" data-slot="image" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="300" height="300">
          </span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__item-title" data-slot="title"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__item-price" data-slot="price"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__item-availability" data-slot="availability"></span>
          {%- comment -%}
            An EXPLICITLY LABELLED remove control, never a swipe (task 21.1): a swipe
            is undiscoverable, impossible with a keyboard, and destructive. It stays
            live in every state, including for a product Shopify has lost, or a
            deleted product could never be cleared (Requirement 7.6).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button class="athoor-portal__item-remove" type="button" data-portal-wishlist-remove data-slot="remove"></button>
          <button class="athoor-portal__action athoor-wishlist__add" type="button" data-portal-wishlist-add data-slot="add"></button>
        </li>
      </template>

      {%- comment -%}
        Requirement 7.11 — the empty state's route to the catalogue. Server-rendered
        so it works before any script runs.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="athoor-portal__empty-action" data-portal-empty-action>
        <a class="athoor-portal__action" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">Browse fragrances</a>
      </p>

    {%- when 'activity' -%}
      <template data-portal-row="activity">
        <li class="athoor-portal__row athoor-activity__row">
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-description" data-slot="description"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-points" data-slot="points"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="date"></span>
          {%- comment -%}
            Requirement 9.5 — a route to the order for an order-related entry. The
            module REMOVES this when the entry has no order reference, rather than
            rendering a link to nothing.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <a class="athoor-activity__order-link" data-slot="order-link" href="#" hidden></a>
        </li>
      </template>

      <button class="athoor-portal__more" type="button" data-portal-more-activity hidden>
        Show earlier activity
      </button>

      {%- comment -%}
        Requirement 9.10 — the empty state describes how points are earned, rather
        than only stating that there is nothing.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="athoor-portal__empty-action" data-portal-empty-action>
        You earn points on every order, and on your first purchase. Points appear here
        as soon as an order is paid.
      </p>

    {%- when 'rewards' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Task 22.1. The balance is the only Numeral use on the page, and the progress
        bar carries `role="progressbar"` WITH an adjacent text statement — because
        `aria-valuenow` is not a sentence a sighted customer can read (§20.4).

        The tier badge carries its tier as TEXT, not as a colour, so it survives
        forced-colours mode and colour blindness (Requirement 17.8).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <header class="athoor-rewards__summary">
        <p class="athoor-portal__eyebrow">Your points</p>
        <p class="athoor-rewards__balance athoor-portal__row-points" data-slot="balance">0</p>
        <p class="athoor-rewards__tier"><span class="athoor-rewards__badge" data-slot="tier"></span> <span data-slot="multiplier"></span></p>

        <div class="athoor-rewards__progress" data-portal-progress>
          <span class="athoor-rewards__progress-fill" data-portal-progress-fill></span>
        </div>
        <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="progress-text"></p>
        <p class="athoor-rewards__expiring" data-portal-expiring hidden></p>
      </header>

      {%- comment -%}
        The issued code panel. 18 px monospace-tabular with a 44 px copy control and
        how to use it (task 22.3). Hidden until a redemption succeeds.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="athoor-rewards__code-panel" data-portal-code-panel hidden>
        <p class="athoor-portal__eyebrow">Your reward</p>
        <p class="athoor-rewards__code" data-portal-code></p>
        <button class="athoor-portal__action" type="button" data-portal-copy-code hidden>Copy code</button>
        <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta">Enter this at checkout to apply your reward.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="athoor-rewards__wait athoor-portal__row-meta" data-portal-wait hidden></p>

      <a class="athoor-portal__action athoor-rewards__activity-link" href="/pages/my-athoor-activity">
        Points activity
      </a>

      {%- comment -%}
        Confirmation reuses the ONE sheet implementation of task 18.5 — native
        `<dialog>`, focus to the heading, focus returned on close, `Esc` and a
        visible dismiss control (Requirement 25.8). No second modal system.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <dialog class="athoor-portal__sheet" data-portal-redeem-sheet aria-labelledby="AthoorRedeemTitle">
        <div class="athoor-portal__sheet-inner">
          <h2 class="athoor-portal__sheet-title" id="AthoorRedeemTitle" data-portal-sheet-heading>Confirm your reward</h2>
          <p data-slot="sheet-cost"></p>
          <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="sheet-after"></p>
          <button class="athoor-portal__action" type="button" data-portal-redeem-confirm>Confirm</button>
          <button class="athoor-portal__sheet-dismiss" type="button" data-portal-sheet-dismiss>Cancel</button>
        </div>
      </dialog>

      <template data-portal-row="reward">
        {%- comment -%}
          A card, and one of only three §18.5 permits: a reward is a discrete offer
          with a price and an action, so it needs a boundary to be a unit.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <li class="athoor-portal__card">
          <span class="athoor-portal__card-value" data-slot="value"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__card-cost" data-slot="cost"></span>
          {%- comment -%}
            The server's own `additionalPointsRequired`, rendered as given. This
            module performs no threshold comparison (task 22.2).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="eligibility"></span>
          <button class="athoor-portal__card-action" type="button" data-slot="redeem"></button>
        </li>
      </template>

    {%- when 'fragrance' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Task 24.1 — §12.5's provenance separation, structurally rather than as a
        caption bolted on afterwards.

        TWO SEPARATE `<section>` ELEMENTS, never interleaved. A declared preference
        is a statement the customer made and can correct; a derived signal is our
        reading of their behaviour and may simply be wrong — a gift bought for
        someone else looks exactly like a purchase for oneself. Mixing them in one
        list would present our arithmetic as their words.

        Each block carries its provenance in its ACCESSIBLE NAME as well as its
        heading, so the difference is not colour or layout alone (Requirement 17.8),
        and every item carries `data-provenance` so the separation can be asserted
        mechanically rather than reviewed by eye (task 24.3).

        The derived block has NO edit control anywhere in this arm. Editing an
        inference is meaningless: the customer would be correcting our arithmetic
        instead of stating a preference. The promotion control is the honest
        alternative — it moves the value into the declared store, where it becomes
        their statement and is thereafter stable (§12.5 rule 4).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <section
        class="athoor-fragrance__block"
        data-portal-declared
        aria-labelledby="AthoorFragranceDeclaredTitle"
        hidden
      >
        <h2 class="athoor-fragrance__heading" id="AthoorFragranceDeclaredTitle">You told us</h2>
        <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta">Select what you like. Your choices are saved as you make them.</p>
        <div class="athoor-fragrance__dimensions" data-portal-dimensions></div>
      </section>
      {%- comment -%}
        One dimension's pill set. The LEGEND carries the dimension name, so a screen
        reader announces which group a pill belongs to — a bare list of pills is
        unusable without it. `<fieldset>` because these are grouped controls.

        Per-dimension empty states are invitations, never errors and never a hidden
        block (Requirement 12.7): a dimension with nothing selected still renders its
        options with a prompt.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <template data-portal-row="dimension">
        <fieldset class="athoor-fragrance__dimension">
          <legend class="athoor-portal__eyebrow" data-slot="legend"></legend>
          <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="prompt"></p>
          <div class="athoor-fragrance__pills" data-slot="pills" role="group"></div>
        </fieldset>
      </template>
      {%- comment -%}
        One selectable value. `aria-pressed` rather than a checkbox, because the
        control's own label is the value and a toggle button states its state without
        needing a second visible label. 44 px minimum.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <template data-portal-row="pill">
        <button
          class="athoor-fragrance__pill"
          type="button"
          data-portal-pill
          data-provenance="declared"
          aria-pressed="false"
        ><span data-slot="label"></span></button>
      </template>
      {%- comment -%}
        The derived block. Absent ENTIRELY when there is no behavioural history
        rather than shown empty (§12.6), which is why the module reveals it instead
        of the template rendering it visible.

        The accessible name names the SOURCE, not just the fact of derivation
        (§12.5 rule 2), and the one-line basis explanation beneath it names the
        inputs (§12.5 rule 3).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <section
        class="athoor-fragrance__block athoor-fragrance__block--derived"
        data-portal-derived
        aria-labelledby="AthoorFragranceDerivedTitle"
        hidden
      >
        <h2 class="athoor-fragrance__heading" id="AthoorFragranceDerivedTitle">
          From your own activity — your orders, saved items and recent views
        </h2>
        <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-portal-basis></p>
        <p class="athoor-fragrance__insight" data-portal-insight hidden></p>
        <div class="athoor-fragrance__derived" data-portal-derived-groups></div>
      </section>
      {%- comment -%}
        One derived value. Read-only text plus an OPTIONAL promotion control, which
        the module removes when the value is already declared or is not in the
        server's vocabulary — a control that would be rejected is worse than none.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <template data-portal-row="derived">
        <li class="athoor-portal__row" data-provenance="derived">
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-description" data-slot="value"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-slot="evidence"></span>
          <button class="athoor-portal__action" type="button" data-portal-promote data-slot="promote"></button>
        </li>
      </template>
      <template data-portal-row="derived-group">
        <div class="athoor-fragrance__derived-group">
          <h3 class="athoor-portal__eyebrow" data-slot="legend"></h3>
          <ul class="athoor-fragrance__derived-list" role="list" data-slot="list"></ul>
        </div>
      </template>
      {%- comment -%}
        The recently-viewed strip. Its own block, and derived by nature — the ids come
        from the customer's own view history — so every item carries the derived
        marker and there is no control on it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <section class="athoor-fragrance__block" data-portal-recent aria-labelledby="AthoorFragranceRecentTitle" hidden>
        <h2 class="athoor-fragrance__heading" id="AthoorFragranceRecentTitle">Recently viewed</h2>
        <ul class="athoor-fragrance__recent" role="list" data-portal-recent-list></ul>
      </section>
      <template data-portal-row="recent">
        <li class="athoor-fragrance__recent-item" data-provenance="derived">
          <a data-slot="link" href="#">
            <span class="athoor-portal__image-box">
              <img class="athoor-portal__image" data-slot="image" alt="" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            </span>
            <span data-slot="title"></span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </template>
      {%- comment -%}
        Requirement 12.6 — no preferences and no history at all. Leads with the
        three-question quickest path (§12.6): families, intensity, occasions. An
        invitation, not an apology.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="athoor-portal__empty-action" data-portal-empty-action>
        <p>Tell us your taste in three answers: which families you like, how strong you wear it, and when.</p>
      </div>
    {%- when 'referrals' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Task 23.1. NOT ONE NUMBER APPEARS IN THIS ARM. Every points figure, stage
        name, qualification sentence and state word is written by the section module
        from `GET /v1/referral` (Requirements 10.10, 10.11), so a change to the
        programme's economics reaches the customer without a theme deployment
        (Requirement 10.13). That is also why there is no "earn N points" heading
        here, however much more inviting a concrete figure would read — and why this
        comment states the amount as `N` rather than the number, since the gate
        inspects the file and is right to.

        No referred person's name, email or identifier has anywhere to go: the stage
        row has four slots and all four are programme-level, and the DTO carries no
        such field to begin with (Requirement 10.7).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <header class="athoor-referrals__invite">
        <p class="athoor-portal__eyebrow">Your code</p>
        {%- comment -%}
          The code at 18 px monospace-tabular so it can be read aloud or copied by
          eye, matching the redemption code panel. Empty until the response lands —
          never a placeholder that looks like a real code.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="athoor-referrals__code" data-portal-referral-code></p>
        <p class="athoor-referrals__link athoor-portal__row-meta" data-portal-referral-link hidden></p>
        <div class="athoor-referrals__controls">
          {%- comment -%}
            Copy is always offered; SHARE is revealed by the module only where
            `navigator.share` exists (Requirement 10.3), because a control that does
            nothing is worse than no control. Both are 44 px.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button class="athoor-portal__action" type="button" data-portal-referral-copy hidden>
            Copy your link
          </button>
          <button class="athoor-portal__action" type="button" data-portal-referral-share hidden>
            Share
          </button>
        </div>
        {%- comment -%}
          The confirmation is ANNOUNCED as well as shown (task 23.2) — a clipboard
          write is invisible, and a sighted-only tick tells a screen-reader user
          nothing.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="athoor-portal__row-meta" data-portal-referral-copy-result hidden></p>
      </header>
      {%- comment -%}
        Programme totals (Requirement 10.4): successful, pending, and points earned.
        Values are written by the module; the labels are the only fixed text.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="athoor-referrals__totals" data-portal-referral-totals role="list" hidden>
        <li class="athoor-referrals__total">
          <span class="athoor-portal__eyebrow">Successful</span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-points" data-slot="successful"></span>
        </li>
        <li class="athoor-referrals__total">
          <span class="athoor-portal__eyebrow">Pending</span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-points" data-slot="pending"></span>
        </li>
        <li class="athoor-referrals__total">
          <span class="athoor-portal__eyebrow">Points earned</span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-points" data-slot="credited"></span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="athoor-referrals__heading" data-portal-referral-stages-heading hidden>How it works</h2>
      <template data-portal-row="stage">
        <li class="athoor-portal__row">
          <span class="athoor-portal__eyebrow" data-slot="name"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-description" data-slot="qualification"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-status" data-slot="state"></span>
          <span class="athoor-portal__row-points" data-slot="points"></span>
        </li>
      </template>
      {%- comment -%}
        The manual code-entry fallback (Requirement 10.1 / task 23.1). Revealed only
        on an explicit `wasReferred === false` — never on a missing field, because
        offering the form to someone who has already been credited invites a
        rejection we could have avoided asking for.

        A real `<form>` so Enter submits and the control is a submit button. The
        message region is `aria-live` and linked by `aria-describedby`, so a
        rejection reaches a screen reader without moving focus away from the input.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <form class="athoor-referrals__claim" data-portal-referral-claim hidden novalidate>
        <h2 class="athoor-referrals__heading" id="AthoorReferralClaimTitle">Were you invited?</h2>
        <label class="athoor-referrals__label" for="AthoorReferralClaimInput">Enter your friend's code</label>
        <input
          class="athoor-referrals__input"
          id="AthoorReferralClaimInput"
          name="referralCode"
          type="text"
          autocomplete="off"
          autocapitalize="characters"
          spellcheck="false"
          maxlength="64"
          aria-describedby="AthoorReferralClaimMessage"
        >
        <button class="athoor-portal__action" type="submit" data-portal-referral-claim-submit>Apply code</button>
        <p
          class="athoor-referrals__message"
          id="AthoorReferralClaimMessage"
          data-portal-referral-claim-message
          aria-live="polite"
          hidden
        ></p>
      </form>
      {%- comment -%}
        Requirement 10.8 — the empty state carries the CODE and an invitation, not an
        apology. Server-rendered so it is present before any script runs; the module
        reveals it and fills the code.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="athoor-portal__empty-action" data-portal-empty-action>
        Share your code and you will both be rewarded when your friend joins.
      </p>
  {%- endcase -%}
</section>
